<title>GERMANY: German 10-mth gross TV ad revs rise 13.4 pct.</title>
<headline>German 10-mth gross TV ad revs rise 13.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gross advertising revenues for the German television industry rose 13.4 percent to 8.7 billion marks in the first ten months of 1996 from the same period a year earlier, the IPA Plus agency said on Monday.</p>
<p>The agency, publishing data provided by Dun and Bradstreet's Nielsen research unit, gave the following details in its latest report on advertising revenue from January to October. (All figures in millions of marks unless stated.)</p>
<p>				 AD REVS	MKT SHR	 AD REVS</p>
<p>				Jan-Oct 96    Oct 96	Jan-Oct 95</p>
<p>COMMERCIAL BROADCASTERS  RTL			  2,641	  30.4 pct	2,336</p>
<p> SAT 1			2,096	  24.1 pct	2,001</p>
<p> PRO 7			1,889	  21.7 pct	1,607</p>
<p> RTL 2			  461	   5.3 pct	  361</p>
<p> Kabel 1			261	   3.0 pct	  230</p>
<p> VOX			    232	   2.7 pct	  134</p>
<p> DSF			    157	   1.8 pct	  149</p>
<p> N-TV			   113	   1.3 pct	   91</p>
<p> SUPER-RTL		    74.5	  0.9 pct	  12.8</p>
<p>PUBLIC BROADCASTERS  ARD			    373	   4.3 pct	  377</p>
<p> ZDF			    387	   4.5 pct	  364</p>
<p>TOTAL			 8,687	   100 pct	7,663</p>
<p>NOTE - Data compiled by Nielsen S+P, the German subsidiary of Nielsen. Market share reflects share of advertising revenue.</p>
<p>-- William Boston, Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
